//@version=6
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// H Ticks — Powell Model C  (indicator C: a separate indicator; A and B are untouched)
// RESEARCH MODEL. PROFITABILITY IS UNPROVEN. These are OUR research rules, NOT Powell's official rules.
// Everything below is a simulation on completed 1-minute candles. It is not a promise, not broker results, and no
// drawdown or win-rate figure shown here is verified performance.
//
// REQUIRES A STANDARD 1-MINUTE CHART (NQ / MNQ primary). Other timeframes or synthetic candles show a warning only.
//
// STATE MACHINE (per New York calendar day, Mon-Fri):
//   WAITING -> OPEN_CAPTURED -> MANIPULATION_QUALIFIED -> REVERSAL_CONFIRMED -> (per model) ENTRY_PENDING -> POSITION_OPEN -> COMPLETE
//   plus EXPIRED and INELIGIBLE / INVALIDATED with the reason recorded.
//   1. The exact open of the 10:00 candle is captured when that candle CLOSES (never backdated).
//   2. A manipulation qualifies when a candle (open times 10:00 .. before 10:10) trades far enough from the open
//      (ATR mode: 0.5 x ATR(14) frozen from the last candle before 10:00; or fixed 15 points). Short = above the open,
//      long = below. A candle crossing both thresholds is ambiguous: skipped by default.
//   3. Reversal = N consecutive closes (default 2) back through the open on candles AFTER the manipulation candle
//      (a manipulation and its reversal can never share a candle). The manipulation extreme is then FROZEN.
//   4. Three entry models are simulated independently (shadow trades); only the selected one raises alerts.
//        A plain retest: a limit at the 10am open, eligible from the next candle.
//        B retest + iFVG: a frozen 3-candle FVG formed after 10:00 must be inverted by a close, then the same limit.
//        C Fib overlap + rejection: the open must sit in the 61.8-79% retracement of the manipulation leg, then a
//          rejection candle sets a precision limit at the midpoint of its wick. (OUR experimental variant.)
//   5. Stop beyond the frozen manipulation extreme + buffer (default 2 ticks); trades wider than the cap (default 80
//      ticks) are REJECTED, never squeezed. Target 1R by default (2R or frozen opposing liquidity selectable).
//   6. Pending orders are cancelled at the entry cutoff (10:45); an open position is closed at the 11:00 candle open.
//
// TWO EXECUTION VARIANTS (simulated independently; only the selected one raises alerts):
//   STANDARD  = the 10am reversal / retest execution above (entry models A, B, C and the experimental C-wick) with its structural stop.
//   PRECISION = the SAME validated directional setup (open captured, manipulation, reversal confirmed, filters, cutoff), but it does NOT
//               enter at the reversal. It waits for its own LOCAL trigger on a later completed candle: a confirmed rejection candle and/or a
//               secondary sweep of a confirmed local pivot, inside a band around the 10am open (optionally also inside the Fib overlap).
//               The stop is the trigger candle's own extreme +/- a buffer (a genuine local invalidation), capped in ticks and never
//               compressed; the target is the nearest UNSWEPT opposing liquidity level known when the order is armed (or a fixed R);
//               trades below the minimum planned R are skipped. Retries are NOT implemented: one candidate per variant per day.
//   Mapping: the old entry models are all part of STANDARD. Nothing was removed; with Precision off, Standard runs exactly as before.
//
// Statistics from a handful of days (even 16) cannot show an edge; a small stop with a large planned R does NOT mean small drawdown.
// EXECUTION SIMULATION (OHLC limits, stated plainly):
//   - A limit fills when a LATER candle touches it (or trades 1 tick through it if the strict setting is on). The fill price
//     is the limit price: no price improvement is ever credited.
//   - A candle whose open already lies beyond the frozen manipulation extreme invalidates a pending order instead of filling it.
//   - If one candle contains the fill AND both stop and target, or a later candle contains BOTH stop and target, the order of
//     events is unknowable from OHLC: the trade is flagged AMBIGUOUS and counted as a loss (conservative) by default.
//   - On the fill candle a target touch is ignored (it may have happened before the fill); a stop touch counts (it must follow
//     the fill because price crosses the limit first). MAE / MFE from such candles are flagged as uncertain.
//   - Gap through the stop exits at the open (worse than the stop); gap through the target exits at the target (no improvement).
//   - Slippage is applied adversely to the entry, stop and time exits (not to target limits); commissions are per contract per side.
//   - No intrabar or tick data is used. One-minute OHLC cannot show tick precision.
//
// PRESETS (Settings -> "10. Preset"):
//   CONTEXTUAL (Powell guide) [default] = the context engine: timestamped liquidity levels -> sweep of a PRE-EXISTING level -> CISD (a later close through the
//     first open of the opposing run into the sweep) -> price areas (FVG / order block / breaker / rejection block / iFVG) -> execution.
//       STANDARD  = limit at the CE of the selected area; stop beyond the FULL sweep extreme + buffer; target = nearest unswept opposing liquidity known at arming.
//       PRECISION = same setup, refined by sub-methods (they are NOT extra variants): Fib 0.705 of the leg (sweep extreme -> first confirmed swing after the CISD,
//                   stop beyond 0.79 + buffer) or a local rejection CE (entry = midpoint of a completed local rejection wick inside the parent area).
//   LEGACY 10am = the earlier 10:00 open retest engine below, kept unchanged and selectable.
//   Provenance: [GUIDE] concept described in the guide, [OURS] our mechanical interpretation, [OPT] optional experimental filter, [ENG] engineering approximation.
//   These are NOT Powell's official rules. Higher-timeframe candles are aggregated from the 1m chart and used only after they complete.
// Verification status: reviewed and text-/model-tested only (Python model of the logic). NOT compiled in TradingView, NOT chart-tested.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
indicator("H Ticks — Powell Model C", shorttitle = "H Ticks C", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 500)

const string TZ = "America/New_York"
const int NS = 9
const int NL = 5
const int NF = 15
const string G1 = "1. Times (New York, DST-aware)"
const string G2 = "2. Manipulation and reversal"
const string G3 = "3. Optional liquidity-sweep filter (OFF = baseline)"
const string G4 = "4. Entry model"
const string G5 = "5. Stop, target, risk"
const string G6 = "6. Simulation assumptions"
const string G7 = "7. Display"
const string G8 = "8. Alerts"
const string G0 = "0. Execution variant"
const string G9 = "9. Precision variant (Rejection / Sweep)"

// ───────────────────────────────────────────── INPUTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
string inVariant = input.string("Standard", "Execution variant (selected: alerts, planned lines)", options = ["Standard", "Precision"], group = G0, tooltip = "Standard = the 10am reversal / retest execution (entry models A, B, C below). Precision = wait for a local rejection / secondary sweep after the same setup, with a local stop.")
bool inShowBoth = input.bool(true, "Display both variants on the chart (when both are simulated)", group = G0)
bool inCmpVar = input.bool(false, "Compare both variants' statistics (simulate Standard AND Precision)", group = G0, tooltip = "OFF = only the selected variant is simulated, so Standard behaves exactly as before. ON = both are simulated independently with separate equity and statistics.")
string inORs = input.session("0930-1000", "Opening range (candle OPEN times, end exclusive)", group = G1, tooltip = "Default 09:30-09:59. Frozen when the 10:00 candle closes. Used only for the optional sweep filter and the liquidity target.")
string inMan = input.session("1000-1010", "10am open candle / initial-manipulation window (candle OPEN times, end exclusive)", group = G1, tooltip = "The START is the candle whose exact open is captured (10:00). The first qualifying manipulation must be on a candle that opens in this window (default 10:00-10:09).")
string inCut = input.session("1045-1100", "Entry cutoff -> time exit (NY)", group = G1, tooltip = "FIRST time = entry cutoff: pending entries are cancelled, no new fills. SECOND time = any remaining position is closed at that candle's open (reported as a time exit).")
string inThr = input.string("ATR", "Manipulation threshold mode", options = ["ATR", "Fixed points"], group = G2, tooltip = "Initial research setting, NOT optimised. ATR mode uses ATR frozen from the last completed candle before the 10:00 open, so the manipulation can never inflate its own threshold.")
float inFixed = input.float(15.0, "Fixed threshold (points)", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = G2)
float inAtrM = input.float(0.5, "ATR multiple", minval = 0.05, step = 0.05, group = G2)
int inAtrLen = input.int(14, "ATR length (1m)", minval = 1, group = G2)
int inRevN = input.int(2, "Consecutive closes through the open to confirm the reversal", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = G2, tooltip = "Counted only on candles AFTER the manipulation candle; the count resets if a close fails the condition.")
string inAmbInit = input.string("Skip day", "A first candle that crosses both thresholds", options = ["Skip day", "Use larger excursion"], group = G2)
bool inMaxOn = input.bool(false, "Maximum manipulation-size filter (OFF = baseline)", group = G2, tooltip = "Size is ALWAYS recorded in points and ATR multiples. When ON, a candidate larger than the limit is invalidated at reversal confirmation.")
float inMaxPts = input.float(60.0, "Maximum size (points, used in Fixed mode)", minval = 1.0, group = G2)
float inMaxAtr = input.float(4.0, "Maximum size (ATR multiples, used in ATR mode)", minval = 0.1, group = G2)
bool inSweep = input.bool(false, "Require a post-10am liquidity sweep", group = G3, tooltip = "Short: price must exceed an eligible HIGH by the minimum, then close back below it by the reversal confirmation. Long mirrors. Levels must exist BEFORE they are swept; a sweep before 10:00 is context only. Asia/London levels are NOT implemented.")
int inSweepTk = input.int(1, "Minimum sweep distance (ticks)", minval = 1, group = G3)
bool inLvOR = input.bool(true, "Eligible: frozen opening-range high/low", group = G3)
bool inLvPD = input.bool(true, "Eligible: previous completed regular-session high/low (09:30-16:00)", group = G3, tooltip = "Used only when that session had all 390 one-minute candles.")
string inModel = input.string("A: plain retest", "Selected entry model (alerts + planned lines)", options = ["A: plain retest", "B: retest + iFVG", "C: Fib overlap + rejection"], group = G4)
bool inCompare = input.bool(false, "Comparison mode: simulate A, B, C and C-wick independently", group = G4, tooltip = "OFF = only the selected model is simulated. ON = every model keeps its own independent statistics. Only the selected model raises alerts.")
string inCStop = input.string("Manipulation extreme", "Model C stop policy", options = ["Manipulation extreme", "Rejection wick (experimental)"], group = G4, tooltip = "The wick-stop variant is EXPERIMENTAL and always reported as its own column (C-wick).")
bool inStrict = input.bool(false, "Stricter fill: require trade-through (1 tick beyond the limit)", group = G4, tooltip = "OFF = a touch fills (a simulation assumption, not guaranteed execution).")
int inBuf = input.int(2, "Stop buffer (ticks)", minval = 0, group = G5)
int inMaxStop = input.int(80, "Maximum stop distance (ticks); wider setups are REJECTED", minval = 1, group = G5)
string inTgt = input.string("1R", "Target", options = ["1R", "2R", "Opposing liquidity"], group = G5, tooltip = "Opposing liquidity = nearest frozen opening-range / previous-session level beyond the entry on the profit side; no eligible level = the trade is rejected and counted.")
string inSizeMode = input.string("Fixed contracts", "Position sizing", options = ["Fixed contracts", "Fixed cash risk"], group = G6, tooltip = "Fixed cash risk uses the SAME cash risk for every trade (whole contracts only, rounded DOWN; a setup needing less than one contract is rejected). Use it when comparing variants with very different stop sizes.")
int inQty = input.int(1, "Contracts (Fixed contracts mode, whole contracts)", minval = 1, group = G6)
float inCashRisk = input.float(500.0, "Cash risk per trade (USD, Fixed cash risk mode)", minval = 10.0, step = 50.0, group = G6)
float inComm = input.float(0.0, "Commission (USD per contract per side)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = G6)
int inSlip = input.int(0, "Adverse slippage (ticks) on entry, stop and time exits", minval = 0, group = G6)
string inAmbMode = input.string("Loss (conservative)", "Ambiguous trades", options = ["Loss (conservative)", "Exclude from stats"], group = G6)
bool inFunnel = input.bool(true, "Show funnel table", group = G7)
bool inPerf = input.bool(true, "Show performance table", group = G7)
bool inLedger = input.bool(true, "Show trade ledger", group = G7)
int inLedPage = input.int(1, "Ledger page", minval = 1, group = G7)
string inLedModel = input.string("All", "Ledger model", options = ["All", "A", "B", "C", "C-wick", "Precision", "Ctx Standard", "Ctx Precision"], group = G7)
int inDraw = input.int(5, "Days drawn on the chart", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = G7)
bool inVisPlan = input.bool(true, "Draw planned entry / stop / target (selected model)", group = G7)
bool inVisFib = input.bool(true, "Draw frozen Fib zone, levels and rejection wick", group = G7)
bool inVisFvg = input.bool(true, "Draw the frozen FVG (model B)", group = G7)
bool inVisPrec = input.bool(true, "Draw the Precision trigger wick and swept local level", group = G7)
bool inVisBand = input.bool(false, "Draw the Precision band around the 10am open", group = G7)
bool inDebug = input.bool(false, "Debug: log each day's result to Pine Logs", group = G7)
string inPTrig = input.string("Rejection", "Precision trigger", options = ["Rejection", "Secondary sweep", "Either"], group = G9, tooltip = "Rejection = a confirmed rejection candle in the precision area. Secondary sweep = a confirmed local pivot (formed after the reversal) is exceeded and the candle closes back, with the same rejection conditions. Either = whichever comes first; both on one candle is labelled Sweep + Rejection.")
float inBand = input.float(4.0, "Precision band half-width (ticks around the 10am open)", minval = 0.0, step = 1.0, group = G9, tooltip = "A test parameter, not an optimised value.")
bool inPFib = input.bool(false, "Require the band to overlap the frozen 61.8-79% Fib zone", group = G9, tooltip = "Uses the same frozen, causal displacement-leg anchors as model C. The trigger candle must then interact with the band-and-zone overlap.")
bool inPIfvg = input.bool(false, "Require a confirmed iFVG inversion first (model B rules)", group = G9, tooltip = "The latest eligible FVG is frozen at the reversal confirmation; a later close through it must happen BEFORE a trigger candle can qualify (the inverting candle itself cannot trigger).")
float inWick = input.float(0.40, "Minimum rejection-wick share of the candle range", minval = 0.05, maxval = 0.95, step = 0.05, group = G9)
int inPvL = input.int(1, "Local pivot: candles to the left", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = G9)
int inPvR = input.int(1, "Local pivot: candles to the right", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = G9, tooltip = "A pivot becomes known only when the last right-side candle has CLOSED; it can be swept only by a later candle.")
float inMinR = input.float(5.0, "Minimum planned reward:risk", minval = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = G9, tooltip = "Checked on the ROUNDED entry, stop and target. The nearest eligible target below this is skipped; no farther target is substituted.")
int inPStopCap = input.int(40, "Maximum Precision stop distance (ticks)", minval = 1, group = G9, tooltip = "Over the cap = rejected, never compressed.")
int inPBuf = input.int(2, "Precision stop buffer (ticks)", minval = 0, group = G9)
int inPExp = input.int(3, "Precision order expiry (subsequent chart candles)", minval = 1, group = G9)
string inPTgt = input.string("Opposing liquidity", "Precision target", options = ["Opposing liquidity", "Fixed R"], group = G9, tooltip = "Opposing liquidity = nearest UNSWEPT frozen opening-range / previous-session level beyond the entry on the profit side, known when the order is armed. Fixed R is a separate mode and is labelled as such.")
float inPFixR = input.float(5.0, "Fixed R multiple (Fixed R mode)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = G9)
bool inAlSetup = input.bool(true, "Alert: setup ready (reversal confirmed)", group = G8)
bool inAlArm = input.bool(true, "Alert: order armed (simulated limit, NOT a fill)", group = G8)
bool inAlFill = input.bool(true, "Alert: simulated fill", group = G8)
bool inAlInv = input.bool(true, "Alert: invalidation / cancellation", group = G8)
bool inInfo = input.bool(true, "Show the info panel (left)", group = G7)
bool inVisOR = input.bool(true, "Draw the opening-range box", group = G7)
const string G10 = "10. Preset, window, source timeframe (Contextual)"
const string G11 = "11. Context levels (Contextual)"
const string G12 = "12. Bias and optional filters (Contextual)"
const string G13 = "13. Price areas (Contextual)"
const string G14 = "14. Standard execution (Contextual)"
const string G15 = "15. Precision execution (Contextual)"
const string G16 = "16. Daily risk sequence and display (Contextual)"
string inPreset = input.string("Contextual (Powell guide)", "Preset", options = ["Contextual (Powell guide)", "Legacy 10am"], group = G10, tooltip = "Contextual = the new level / sweep / CISD / price-area engine described in the Powell Model C guide (our mechanical interpretation). Legacy 10am = the earlier 10:00 open retest engine, kept unchanged for comparison. Sections 0-9 apply to Legacy; sections 10-16 apply to Contextual.")
string inCxWin = input.session("0930-1100", "Contextual window: orders may be armed from the FIRST time until the SECOND (NY, candle open times)", group = G10, tooltip = "A setup (sweep + reversal) that formed earlier in the trading day stays eligible; no fresh sweep is required after the window opens.")
string inCxHard = input.string("11:00", "Hard exit (NY HH:MM, candle open)", group = G10, tooltip = "Any open position is closed at the open of the first candle at/after this time. Must not be earlier than the window end.")
string inCxTf = input.string("5m", "Source timeframe for sweeps, CISD, areas and swings (built from 1m candles)", options = ["1m", "5m", "15m"], group = G10, tooltip = "All higher-timeframe candles are aggregated from the 1m chart and used only after they COMPLETE, so nothing can repaint or leak.")
int inCxSwTk = input.int(1, "Minimum sweep distance beyond a level (ticks)", minval = 1, group = G10)
int inCxSwAge = input.int(12, "Candles allowed between the sweep and the CISD close", minval = 1, group = G10)
int inCxAgeMin = input.int(480, "A setup expires if no order was armed within (minutes of its CISD)", minval = 10, group = G10)
int inCxExp = input.int(60, "Pending order expiry (subsequent 1m candles)", minval = 1, group = G10)
bool inCxLvPD = input.bool(true, "Level: previous completed trading-day high/low (18:00 to 17:00)", group = G11)
bool inCxLvPS = input.bool(true, "Level: previous completed regular-session high/low (needs all 390 candles)", group = G11)
bool inCxLvCS = input.bool(true, "Level: current-session high/low that stood for the minutes below", group = G11)
int inCsAge = input.int(10, "Current-session extreme must stand for (minutes)", minval = 1, group = G11)
bool inCxLvOR = input.bool(true, "Level: frozen opening range (09:30-09:59 by default; uses the opening-range setting of section 1)", group = G11)
bool inCxLvEQ = input.bool(true, "Level: confirmed equal highs / lows", group = G11)
int inEqTol = input.int(2, "Equal-level tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0, group = G11)
bool inCxLvAS = input.bool(false, "Level: completed Asia range", group = G11)
string inCxAs = input.session("1900-0000", "Asia range (NY)", group = G11)
bool inCxLvLD = input.bool(false, "Level: completed London range", group = G11)
string inCxLd = input.session("0200-0500", "London range (NY)", group = G11)
bool inCxLvPO = input.bool(false, "Level: predefined PO3 accumulation range", group = G11, tooltip = "The range is fixed in advance (below) and becomes a level only when it has COMPLETED. It is never inferred retrospectively.")
string inCxPo = input.session("0000-0600", "PO3 accumulation range (NY)", group = G11)
bool inCxOpens = input.bool(true, "Show the 18:00 / 00:00 / 10:00 opens (reference only, never an entry)", group = G11)
bool inBiasD = input.bool(false, "Filter: Daily prior-range breakout state must agree (NOT a CISD)", group = G12, tooltip = "Prior-range breakout state per timeframe, from COMPLETED candles only: +1 after a close above the previous candle's high, -1 after a close below its low, otherwise it PERSISTS unchanged (0 until the first breakout). It resets to unavailable when that timeframe loses a candle (incomplete data). It is NOT the opposing-delivery-leg CISD used for the setup.")
bool inBias4 = input.bool(false, "Filter: 4H prior-range breakout state must agree", group = G12)
bool inBias1 = input.bool(false, "Filter: 1H prior-range breakout state must agree", group = G12)
bool inBias30 = input.bool(false, "Filter: 30m prior-range breakout state must agree", group = G12)
bool inBias15 = input.bool(false, "Filter: 15m prior-range breakout state must agree", group = G12)
bool inFPo3 = input.bool(false, "Filter: the swept level must be the PO3 range (enable the PO3 level too)", group = G12)
bool inFConf = input.bool(false, "Filter: parent area must overlap another eligible area of a different type", group = G12)
bool inFIfvg = input.bool(false, "Filter: require a confirmed iFVG among the eligible areas", group = G12)
bool inFChop = input.bool(false, "Filter: reject choppy markets (efficiency ratio of recent source candles)", group = G12)
int inChopN = input.int(12, "Chop filter: candles", minval = 3, group = G12)
float inChopMin = input.float(0.25, "Chop filter: minimum efficiency ratio", minval = 0.01, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = G12)
bool inFCe = input.bool(false, "Filter: reject if same-side liquidity sits within N points beyond the entry (engineered-liquidity proximity)", group = G12, tooltip = "Our reading of the guide's roughly 2-point idea. Optional research filter.")
float inCeDist = input.float(2.0, "Engineered-liquidity proximity (points)", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = G12)
string inSmt = input.string("Off", "SMT divergence (reversal role only)", options = ["Off", "Reversal"], group = G12, tooltip = "Reversal role: at the sweep the peer index must have FAILED to take its own comparable extreme. The target role is NOT implemented.")
string inSmtSym = input.string("CME_MINI:ES1!", "SMT peer symbol", group = G12)
int inSmtLook = input.int(60, "SMT comparison look-back (1m candles before the sweep)", minval = 10, maxval = 200, group = G12)
bool inAFvg = input.bool(true, "Area: FVG (3 candles, usable once the third closed)", group = G13)
bool inAOb = input.bool(true, "Area: order block (last opposite candle before the displacement that confirmed the CISD)", group = G13)
bool inABrk = input.bool(true, "Area: breaker (the broken block, confirmed by a CLOSE through it)", group = G13)
bool inARb = input.bool(true, "Area: rejection block (our thresholds; not attributed to Powell)", group = G13)
bool inAIf = input.bool(true, "Area: iFVG (a gap inverted by a close beyond its opposite side)", group = G13)
float inRbWick = input.float(0.50, "Rejection block: minimum wick share of the range", minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.95, step = 0.05, group = G13)
float inRbBody = input.float(0.40, "Rejection block: maximum body share of the range", minval = 0.05, maxval = 0.9, step = 0.05, group = G13)
int inIfLook = input.int(12, "iFVG: the gap may have formed up to this many source candles before the sweep", minval = 1, group = G13)
string inPoi = input.string("None", "Selected higher-timeframe POI (areas overlapping it are preferred)", options = ["None", "15m FVG", "1H FVG"], group = G13)
int inCxBuf = input.int(2, "Standard stop buffer beyond the sweep extreme (ticks)", minval = 0, group = G14)
int inCxCap = input.int(200, "Standard maximum stop (ticks); wider setups are REJECTED", minval = 1, group = G14)
float inCxMinR = input.float(3.0, "Standard minimum planned reward:risk (checked on rounded prices)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = G14)
string inCxTgt = input.string("Opposing liquidity", "Target", options = ["Opposing liquidity", "Fixed R"], group = G14, tooltip = "Opposing liquidity = nearest UNSWEPT level known when the order is armed, frozen with the stop. No target = the setup is rejected and counted; no farther target is substituted. Fixed R is a separate testing mode.")
float inCxFixR = input.float(3.0, "Fixed R multiple (Fixed R mode)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = G14)
bool inPFibOn = input.bool(true, "Precision method: Fib 0.705 entry", group = G15)
bool inPRejOn = input.bool(true, "Precision method: local rejection CE entry", group = G15)
float inFibE = input.float(0.705, "Fib entry ratio", minval = 0.3, maxval = 0.95, step = 0.005, group = G15)
float inFibS = input.float(0.79, "Fib stop-reference ratio (stop sits beyond this + buffer)", minval = 0.4, maxval = 0.99, step = 0.005, group = G15)
int inCxPv = input.int(2, "Swing strength for the Fib anchor (candles each side)", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = G15, tooltip = "The anchor is the FIRST confirmed swing after the CISD. It is known only when its last right-side candle closes, and is never back-dated.")
bool inFibArea = input.bool(false, "Fib filter: the 0.705 entry must lie inside the selected parent area", group = G15)
int inCxPCap = input.int(80, "Precision maximum stop (ticks)", minval = 1, group = G15)
int inCxPBuf = input.int(2, "Precision stop buffer (ticks)", minval = 0, group = G15)
float inCxPMinR = input.float(3.0, "Precision minimum planned reward:risk (set 5 for the 5R research filter)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = G15)
string inRejTf = input.string("5m", "Local rejection timeframe", options = ["5m", "1m"], group = G15)
float inRejWick = input.float(0.40, "Local rejection: minimum wick share of the range", minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.95, step = 0.05, group = G15)
bool inRejSweep = input.bool(false, "Local rejection: must also sweep the previous local candle's extreme", group = G15)
string inSeq = input.string("One trade per day", "Daily sequence (each variant independently)", options = ["One trade per day", "Win ends day; one 50% retry after a non-win"], group = G16, tooltip = "A win (net R > 0) ends the day. Anything else (loss, ambiguous, flat or time exit) counts as an attempt and allows ONE more trade with 50% of the first trade's actual cash risk (whole contracts, rounded down).")
bool inCxVisCtx = input.bool(true, "Draw live levels and the setup context (sweep, CISD, areas, target)", group = G16)
bool inCxVisAreas = input.bool(false, "Draw every eligible area (otherwise only the selected parent area)", group = G16)
bool inCxVisFib = input.bool(true, "Draw Fib anchors and levels", group = G16)
bool inCxHist = input.bool(true, "Draw historical trades (OFF = latest day only)", group = G16)
bool inCxCompact = input.bool(false, "Compact tables (performance + why-no-trade only)", group = G16)
bool inAlExit = input.bool(true, "Alert: simulated stop / target / time exit", group = G8)
int inCxMiss = input.int(0, "Aggregation: missing 1m candles tolerated per higher-timeframe candle (0 = strict)", minval = 0, maxval = 30, group = G10, tooltip = "A synthetic 5m/15m/30m/1H/4H/Daily candle is published only when all its expected 1m candles are present (scheduled 17:00-18:00 break excluded). TradingView has no bar for a minute without trades, so thin sessions can lose candles; this tolerance trades strictness for availability. Dropped candles are counted in the info panel.")

// ───────────────────────────────────────── TIME AND CHART ─────────────────────────────────────────
f_hhmm(string s) =>
    string t = str.trim(s)
    int p = str.pos(t, ":")
    p >= 0 ? int(str.tonumber(str.substring(t, 0, p))) * 60 + int(str.tonumber(str.substring(t, p + 1, str.length(t)))) : 660

f_mins(string s, int off) =>
    int(str.tonumber(str.substring(s, off, off + 2))) * 60 + int(str.tonumber(str.substring(s, off + 2, off + 4)))

int orS = f_mins(inORs, 0)
int orE = f_mins(inORs, 5)
int openT = f_mins(inMan, 0)
int manE = f_mins(inMan, 5)
int cutT = f_mins(inCut, 0)
int exitT = f_mins(inCut, 5)
bool cfgOk = orS < orE and openT < manE and manE <= cutT and cutT < exitT and orE <= openT
int winS = f_mins(inCxWin, 0)
int cutM = f_mins(inCxWin, 5)
int exitM = f_hhmm(inCxHard)
bool cxCfgOk = winS < cutM and cutM <= exitM and orS < orE
bool isCx = inPreset != "Legacy 10am"
bool cfgAll = isCx ? cxCfgOk : cfgOk

bool supported = chart.is_standard and not timeframe.isticks and timeframe.isminutes and timeframe.multiplier == 1
int chartMs = 60000
float tk = syminfo.mintick
int mOpen = hour(time, TZ) * 60 + minute(time, TZ)
int dkey = year(time, TZ) * 10000 + month(time, TZ) * 100 + dayofmonth(time, TZ)
int dowN = dayofweek(time, TZ)
float atrV = ta.atr(inAtrLen)
float h2 = high[2]
float l2 = low[2]
int t2 = time[2]
int tdk = year(time + 21600000, TZ) * 10000 + month(time + 21600000, TZ) * 100 + dayofmonth(time + 21600000, TZ)
[esH, esL] = request.security(inSmt != "Off" ? inSmtSym : syminfo.tickerid, "1", [high, low])

int stdSel = inModel == "A: plain retest" ? 0 : (inModel == "B: retest + iFVG" ? 1 : (inCStop == "Rejection wick (experimental)" ? 3 : 2))
int selVar = inVariant == "Precision" ? 1 : 0
int selSlot = isCx ? (selVar == 1 ? 6 : 5) : (selVar == 1 ? 4 : stdSel)
int altDraw = inShowBoth ? (selVar == 1 ? stdSel : 4) : -1
bool stdOn = selVar == 0 or inCmpVar
bool precOn = selVar == 1 or inCmpVar
var array<bool> slotOn = array.from(not isCx and stdOn and (inCompare or stdSel == 0), not isCx and stdOn and (inCompare or stdSel == 1), not isCx and stdOn and (inCompare or stdSel == 2), not isCx and stdOn and (inCompare or stdSel == 3), not isCx and precOn, isCx and stdOn, isCx and precOn, isCx and precOn, isCx and precOn)
var array<string> slotNm = array.from("STD-A", "STD-B", "STD-C", "STD-C wick", "PREC", "CTX-STD", "CTX-PREC", "PREC-Fib", "PREC-Rej")

// ───────────────────────────────────────────── TYPES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
type Trade
    int slot
